{"id": "EUVD-2026-62576", "enisaUuid": "c33bd657-da44-339a-9814-6e6b044626c0", "description": "A vulnerability in the web-based management interface of Cisco Unified Intelligence Center could allow an authenticated, local attacker to perform a blind SQL injection attack against an affected device.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to insufficient validation of user-supplied input. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted request to the web-based management interface. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to read the contents of the internal database&nbsp;of an affected device. To exploit this vulnerability, the attacker must have valid user credentials on the affected device.", "datePublished": "2026-08-19T16:22:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T18:23:51", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-cuic-sql-inject-2qbfWSm5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-20327", "GHSA-23r9-9w5h-7769"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19748919-cdc9-3f10-84ed-36bf8d897700", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Intelligence Center", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "15.0(1)"}, {"id": "26e7c9f7-9259-3630-ada7-ad37da73a7d1", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Intelligence Center", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "12.5(1)SU"}, {"id": "2a3b364e-3a6c-3e06-a271-c7cc074fc4e2", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Intelligence Center", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "12.5(1)"}, {"id": "2da65503-0345-3978-84f7-a1311f4a5468", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Intelligence Center", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "11.0(2)"}, {"id": "3284fca5-f5d1-3403-9593-bdc2b060cb51", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Intelligence Center", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "15.0.1_CSCwu05225_ET"}, {"id": "34de